In a commentary of the legal

45:17.133 --> 45:19.500 align:center
system in the 1760s, William

45:19.500 --> 45:20.067 align:center
Blackstone penned the maxim

45:20.067 --> 45:21.567 align:center
that it is better that 10

45:21.567 --> 45:23.200 align:center
guilty persons go free than 1

45:23.200 --> 45:24.200 align:center
innocent person suffer. In the

45:24.200 --> 45:25.833 align:center
1780s, our founding father

45:25.833 --> 45:26.500 align:center
Benjamin Franklin expanded that

45:26.500 --> 45:27.600 align:center
viewpoint to a ratio of 100 to

45:27.600 --> 45:30.133 align:center
1. I am capable of recognizing

45:30.133 --> 45:31.700 align:center
the utility and benefit that

45:31.700 --> 45:32.333 align:center
ALPRs offer law enforcement in

45:32.333 --> 45:34.300 align:center
their efforts to aid society

45:34.300 --> 45:34.967 align:center
and meaningfully reduce crime.

45:34.967 --> 45:36.600 align:center
However, that utility and

45:36.600 --> 45:37.200 align:center
benefit becomes meaningless

45:37.200 --> 45:38.467 align:center
when we, the people's

45:38.467 --> 45:39.000 align:center
constitutional rights are

45:39.000 --> 45:39.600 align:center
infringed and our well-being

45:39.600 --> 45:41.733 align:center
harmed. Just this week, 3 US

45:41.733 --> 45:43.633 align:center
senators, Josh Hawley, Raphael

45:43.633 --> 45:44.200 align:center
Warnock, and our own Kitty

45:44.200 --> 45:46.000 align:center
Britt expressed their concerns

45:46.000 --> 45:46.567 align:center
for the abuse and lack of

45:46.567 --> 45:48.533 align:center
regulation of ALPR networks,

45:48.533 --> 45:49.900 align:center
and I will add that in that

45:49.900 --> 45:50.533 align:center
same congressional hearing, the

45:50.533 --> 45:51.133 align:center
CEOs of four leading ALPR

45:51.133 --> 45:52.900 align:center
companies that were invited to

45:52.900 --> 45:54.633 align:center
testify, yet none felt it was

45:54.633 --> 45:55.300 align:center
important to do so despite the

45:55.300 --> 45:56.800 align:center
tremendous nationwide concern

45:56.800 --> 45:57.500 align:center
about on this topic by citizens

45:57.500 --> 45:59.900 align:center
of all manners of various

45:59.900 --> 46:00.500 align:center
political beliefs this year

46:00.500 --> 46:01.400 align:center
more than 200 cities and

46:01.400 --> 46:02.033 align:center
counties have terminated their

46:02.033 --> 46:03.467 align:center
contracts with ALPR companies,

46:03.467 --> 46:04.133 align:center
and while some of those cities

46:04.133 --> 46:06.067 align:center
signed contracts with a

46:06.067 --> 46:06.800 align:center
different ALPR company assuring

46:06.800 --> 46:08.100 align:center
stricter guardrails and abuse

46:08.100 --> 46:08.833 align:center
detecting audits. More than 100

46:08.833 --> 46:11.700 align:center
walked away from AR. ALPR

46:11.700 --> 46:12.667 align:center
technology entirely to include

46:12.667 --> 46:14.667 align:center
a municipality with a

46:14.667 --> 46:15.300 align:center
population comparable to that

46:15.300 --> 46:17.100 align:center
of Huntsville. Following the US

46:17.100 --> 46:17.667 align:center
Supreme Court ruling this

46:17.667 --> 46:18.233 align:center
summer in Chatri v. United

46:18.233 --> 46:19.333 align:center
States, which is my opinion

46:19.333 --> 46:19.933 align:center
that civil liberties

46:19.933 --> 46:21.933 align:center
organizations have gained

46:21.933 --> 46:22.533 align:center
newfound leverage for pending

46:22.533 --> 46:23.100 align:center
lawsuits that could one day

46:23.100 --> 46:24.500 align:center
soon see ALPR Networks ruled

46:24.500 --> 46:26.267 align:center
unconstitutional at that point

46:26.267 --> 46:26.767 align:center
in time, I would like

46:26.767 --> 46:27.433 align:center
Huntsville to be able to look

46:27.433 --> 46:28.767 align:center
proudly at their history as one

46:28.767 --> 46:30.533 align:center
of the cities which decided

46:30.533 --> 46:31.167 align:center
voluntarily and proactively to

46:31.167 --> 46:33.067 align:center
stop using ALPRs rather than

46:33.067 --> 46:33.667 align:center
being on the wrong side of

46:33.667 --> 46:34.300 align:center
history as a city which only

46:34.300 --> 46:35.433 align:center
did so when compelled by legal

46:35.433 --> 46:37.567 align:center
precedent and judicial mandate.

46:37.567 --> 46:39.500 align:center
With all of this in mind, that

46:39.500 --> 46:40.167 align:center
is, this is why I once more ask

46:40.167 --> 46:41.900 align:center
